DTSTART:20261211T193000Z
DTEND:20261211T203000Z
LOCATION:Asian Culture Center (807 E 10th street\, Bloomington\, IN)
SUMMARY:Asian Cultures Around Campus: Henna Fridays
DESCRIPTION:The term Mehendi is the Indian word for&#160\;Henna\, and it 
 is also the term used to describe the art of applying&#160\;henna.&#160\;
 Come and learn&#160\;the basic designs and application techniques of&#160
 \;Henna&#160\;or&#160\;Mehendi\, which&#160\;is&#160\;used to create temp
 orary tattoos. Please feel free to bring your friends to learn more about
  Desi culture and the significance of&#160\;Mehendi&#160\;in the Indian c
 ulture! If you come with a group of more than 7 members\, please email&#1
 60\;acc@iu.edu&#160\;in advance so we can prepare the henna materials.&#1
 60\;&#160\;&#160\;  &#160\;All Indiana University events\, groups\, activ
 ities\, and&#160\;educational\, cultural\, and historical observances wel
 come all IU students and other members of the Indiana University communit
 y.  &#160\;For more information\, view this event in BeInvolved (https://
 beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12554986).
